  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Government Debt Issuance and Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Creation of a Primary Dealer Network to set forth the criteria for participants acting as debt underwriters and market makers. Banco Central del Uruguay (BCU) currently auctions debt in the domestic market on a regular basis. The bidders are the local commercial banks, and these banks are also the principal price makers in the secondary trading market. There is no formal arrangement between BCU and the banks as to responsibilities or conduct. The creation of a Primary Dealer Network would formalize the roles and responsibilities of all parties. The Network would establish metrics for evaluating performance in both the primary and secondary markets. BCUs debt, while issued domestically, is purchased primarily by the commercial banks and some of their institutional investors. There is a need to broaden the market for this debt. The establishment of a Retail Program for individual investors is intended to reach more investors and to find more stable sources of funding.</narrative>
  </description>
